@*
    _AdminOnboardingBanner.cshtml — the M30 admin onboarding affordance (ADR
    0153, M30·5).

    The GlobalAdmin sibling of the M22 resident _OnboardingBanner (ADR 0132):
    a dismissible banner rendered on every /admin/* page (wired into
    _AdminNav.cshtml, the M29 admin sub-nav scope) that walks a new
    GlobalAdmin to /admin/onboarding.

      - Renders ONLY when the signed-in actor is a GlobalAdmin AND
        AdminOnboarding.CompletedAt is null (M30·5 — the bannerEligible read
        + the GlobalAdmin-gated scope; a non-GlobalAdmin never sees it, and a
        completed admin never sees it). The GlobalAdmin check is the standard
        role read (KumunitaPrincipal.IsGlobalAdmin — the thin-token rule, ADR
        0001-B, never a claim re-derived here); the completion read is the
        IAdminOnboardingService.GetAsync seam — the SAME seam the
        AdminOnboardingController.Index action + the /admin/onboarding view
        call, so the banner + the view resolve to the same value (M30·5).
      - Non-blocking (M30·5): it never gates sign-in; the /admin/onboarding
        route is always reachable for a GlobalAdmin. The close button is a
        *client-side* dismiss only (onboarding-banner.js — a sessionStorage
        flag, never a write to CompletedAt); the only way to clear the banner
        for real is the explicit "mark as complete" POST (M30·4).
      - The copy is the closed adminonboarding.banner.* kw-l set (M30·6, the
        21-key set U05 authored) — never an inline string. The a11y.*
        accessible names are server-resolved (the kw-l TagHelper can't wrap
        an attribute).

    Dismissal is remembered per browser via sessionStorage (the M22
    onboarding-banner.js idiom) — a plain ES module (tsc-built, no bundler),
    CSP-safe (script-src 'self'). The shared .kumunita-onboarding-banner
    class is intentional: onboarding-banner.js selects that class, so the
    single shared module dismisses this banner too (one dismissal mechanism,
    two banners — the resident's and the admin's).
*@
@using Kumunita.Core.AdminOnboarding
@using Kumunita.Web.Security
@inject IAdminOnboardingService AdminOnboarding
@inject Kumunita.Core.Localization.ILocalizationService Localization
@inject Kumunita.Core.Localization.ITranslationProvider Translation
@inject Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.IHttpContextAccessor HttpContextAccessor
@{
    // GlobalAdmin only (M30·5): a non-GlobalAdmin never sees the banner, even
    // if CompletedAt is null. Unauthenticated has no role → no banner.
    bool isGlobalAdmin = User.Identity?.IsAuthenticated == true
        && KumunitaPrincipal.IsGlobalAdmin(User);
    // The completion read (M30·5): the SAME GetAsync seam the controller +
    // the /admin/onboarding view call — best-effort, a missing store / missing
    // row / read failure degrades to null (= not-yet-guided, the floor).
    bool bannerEligible = false;
    if (isGlobalAdmin)
    {
        var completedAt = await AdminOnboarding.GetAsync();
        bannerEligible = completedAt is null;
    }
}
@if (bannerEligible)
{
    // The banner's accessible names are server-resolved (the kw-l TagHelper
    // can't wrap an attribute); the a11y.* floor is the closed M22 set (the
    // region / action / dismiss a11y keys are shared, present in four
    // languages).
    var effLang = await EffectiveLanguageCode.ResolveAsync(HttpContextAccessor.HttpContext?.Request, Localization, Translation);
    string ariaRegion   = await Translation.GetAsync("a11y.onboarding_region", effLang);
    string ariaAction   = await Translation.GetAsync("a11y.onboarding_action", effLang);
    string ariaDismiss  = await Translation.GetAsync("a11y.onboarding_dismiss", effLang);

    <div class="kumunita-onboarding-banner alert alert-secondary alert-dismissible fade show mb-3"
         role="region" aria-label="@ariaRegion">
        <div class="container-fluid py-2 d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
            <span class="me-auto me-2">
                <kw-l key="adminonboarding.banner.text">Finish setting up this community?</kw-l>
            </span>
            <a class="btn btn-sm btn-primary text-nowrap" href="/admin/onboarding"
               aria-label="@ariaAction"><kw-l key="adminonboarding.banner.action">Start setup</kw-l></a>
            <button type="button" class="btn-close"
                    data-dismiss-key="kumunita-onboarding-banner-dismissed"
                    aria-label="@ariaDismiss"></button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script type="module" src="~/js/lib/onboarding-banner.js"></script>
}
